  "caveats": {
    "no_random_draws": "Every arm is one sliced architecture that was then fine-tuned, so each reports a single deterministic accuracy -- the same protocol as exp23's magnitude_recovery, which it is compared with. 1a's 20 random draws prune a dense model, where a draw costs nothing; here a draw would mean a separate recovery run.",
    "aligned_subset": "The 1a checkpoints trained at mask_ratio 0.5, so an aligned set below 50% is the lowest-magnitude subset of SAL's own set, flagged per arm as aligned_is_subset.",
    "drophead_has_no_aligned_set": "DropHead resamples every step, so there is no set it was trained to live without; only a magnitude arm is defined for it.",
    "magnitude_arm_is_reused": "The magnitude+recovery row is read from exp23 rather than retrained, so it is the identical number, not a replication."
  },
